+      "title": "Same *se*, same agreement",
+      "content": "You know the passive *se* from B1 Unit 6: *se* plus a verb in the third person says that something is done without saying who does it. The noun after the verb is the subject of the sentence, so the verb agrees with it in number: *Se vende una casa*, but *Se venden casas*. This lesson shows that the agreement holds whenever you have a noun: after two nouns, with the noun in front of the verb, and after *poder* or *deber* plus an infinitive."
